   184	## A10.5 Attestation selection, in stages — OWNER DECISION, CLARIFY (review A05)
   185	
   186	C5 selects "the verified attestation at the lowest block height in the presented OTS proof" (:144). C6 says "A
   187	selected anchor (C5) beyond the newest pin is `UNVERIFIABLE`", "Every supplied header must be pinned" and "An
   188	unselected attestation without its headers supplies no fact and is not a failure" (:145). "Verified" can be read
   189	with or without pin coverage. The profile already fixes one order (`docs/V1-PROFILE.md` §7.1–§7.2, OWNER
   190	2026-10-14, G05, G07, G23; precedence rows 10–11). This amendment states that order as A9's meaning.
   191	
   192	These stages explain qualification and selection within the existing verifier. They do not replace other
   193	registered checks, their dependencies, or dispatch and reason-code precedence. A failure of an independently
   194	performable required check takes precedence over an unperformable check under A4.2. The header-pool link checks,
   195	OTS grammar and stamp checks, and selected-height transaction/path checks remain unchanged. A stage's UNVERIFIABLE
   196	entry is an unperformable-check result, not an early return that suppresses other checks.
   197	
   198	**Stages**, for each of the receipt, snapshot and git proofs:
   199	1. **Header pool.** Every supplied header, used or not, is checked against the pins. A header at a height with no
   200	   pin gives `UNVERIFIABLE / HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`; a header that differs from its pin gives `INVALID /
   201	   HEADER_CONFLICTS_PIN`.
   202	2. **Qualification ("verified").** A Bitcoin attestation at height h qualifies only if the bundled header at h has
   203	   a merkle root equal to the attestation message, headers h … h+5 are all bundled, each equals its pin, and each
   204	   links to the one before. Pin coverage is part of "verified". A pinned header at h whose merkle root contradicts
   205	   the attestation gives `INVALID / OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH`.
   206	3. **Selection.** The selected anchor is the qualifying attestation at the lowest height h*. T and the confirmation
   207	   count come from h*. A non-qualifying attestation, including one without headers or one beyond the newest pin,
   208	   is never selected; it supplies no fact and is not a failed check, except as stages 1–2 state. A failed check at
   209	   h* never moves selection to a higher height.
   210	4. **No qualifying attestation.** The check is unperformable (`HEADERS_MISSING`, or `ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY` if only
   211	   pending attestations; `SNAPSHOT_NOT_ANCHORED` and `GIT_NOT_ANCHORED` for those proofs). The overall verdict is
   212	   `UNVERIFIABLE` unless another independently performable required check fails, in which case it is `INVALID`
   213	   under A4.2.
   214	
   215	**Cases**, each subject to A4.2 precedence over any other failed check. A qualifying path at h = 100 and a lower,
   216	headerless attestation at h = 90: h* = 100. A sole attestation beyond the newest pin, without headers: stage 4,
   217	unperformable. The same with its headers supplied: stage 1, `HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`, unperformable. So C6's
   218	"selected anchor beyond the newest pin" cannot arise; an anchor beyond the pins makes a check unperformable through
   219	stage 1 or stage 4. The assembled C5 claim cell is in A10.1. The changed sentences are rows 17–18 of A10.7.
